        ^"Mystical Being" DEF {
            ^"Description" STRING "A snow lion is an Otherworldly being of silhouette 3. While they cannot fly vertically, they still ignore the negative effects of terrain. Additionally, once per scene, they may perform a kihō (holy). The kihō counts as succeeding with three bonus successes and :opp::opp:."
        }

        ^"Roar of Emptiness" DEF {
            ^"Description" STRING "Once per scene, a snow lion may roar. Everyone within range 5 of the snow lion must succeed on a TN 4 Meditation check (Fire 5, Void 3) or gain the Disoriented condition and suffer 3 strife. If they succeed, they remove 3 strife instead."
        }

        RULES {
            #L5RCW35287dc49c001637835611: snow_lion "Snow Lion: With white fur and a turquoise mane, this being with a round face and a jaw in a perpetual grin can be found in the mountains, leaping from peak to peak. They do not fly, but their feet never touch the ground. The Ujik associate the snow lion with strength, joy, and playfulness. Some who follow Shinseism believe that its roar imparts insights toward Enlightenment. When a seeker of truth climbs one of the highest mountain peaks, that seeker might end up playing tag or fetch with a snow lion—and on occasion, a snow lion might steal such a person's belongings, necessitating a chase, only to disappear seemingly into thin air."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 156)
    ^"Wind Horse" DEF {
